# DynamicRecordForm Refactoring Walkthrough

The massive `DynamicRecordForm` Livewire component has been successfully refactored. Its extensive business logic responsibilities have been isolated into clear, maintainable domain Service classes under the `App\Services` namespace.

---

## 🛠️ Changes Made

### 1. Extracted Domain Service Classes
Four new service classes were created to take on specific responsibilities:
- **[TokenMintingService](file:///d:/git-PRMS%20Dev/PRMS_Dev/prms/app/Services/TokenMintingService.php)**: 
  - Handles secure generation, prefixing, and cleanup of editor tokens.
- **[RecordCommentService](file:///d:/git-PRMS%20Dev/PRMS_Dev/prms/app/Services/RecordCommentService.php)**: 
  - Handles creating and deleting comments linked to records.
- **[RecordSaveService](file:///d:/git-PRMS%20Dev/PRMS_Dev/prms/app/Services/RecordSaveService.php)**: 
  - Manages record updates/creation, file uploads, and attachment versioning arrays.
- **[RecordApprovalService](file:///d:/git-PRMS%20Dev/PRMS_Dev/prms/app/Services/RecordApprovalService.php)**: 
  - Encapsulates workflow approval actions (approving, submitting, returning for revision, branch forwarding, and marking reviews done) along with the associated authorization guards and database/mail notifications.

### 2. Streamlined Livewire Component
- **[DynamicRecordForm.php](file:///d:/git-PRMS%20Dev/PRMS_Dev/prms/app/Livewire/Builder/DynamicRecordForm.php)**:
  - Cleaned up heavy dependency list imports.
  - Delegated the actual work inside `mount()`, `persistRecord()`, `submitForApproval()`, `approve()`, `forwardToBranch()`, `returnForRevision()`, `markReviewDone()`, `addComment()`, and `deleteComment()` to the injected Services using Laravel's robust `app(...)` container resolver.
  - Eliminated helper authorization/checking methods (such as `canEditRecord()`, `canAct()`, `canReview()`) from the component, routing them through the `RecordApprovalService`.

